{
  "_comment": "Ordered panel classifier. FIRST HIT WINS — order is meaningful. Keywords are matched case-insensitively as substrings against the analyte's English name, abbreviation, key and local-language name joined together. Bilingual (EN + RU) on purpose: lab exports are rarely in one language. Add your own language by appending keywords.",
  "_ordering_note": "INFLAMMATION must precede PROTEINS, otherwise 'C-Reactive PROTEIN' is captured by the PROTEINS rule. This is the kind of ordering bug that only shows up on real data.",
